    {
      "heading": "With and against the wind",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A plane flies 1800 kilometres with the wind in 3 hours.",
          "write": "p + w = 1800 ÷ 3 = 600",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 240,
            "alt": "Speed with and against the wind",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 60,
                "y": 90,
                "x2": 500,
                "y2": 90,
                "color": "blue",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 70,
                "text": "plane + wind = 600",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "blue",
                "change": "add",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 500,
                "y": 190,
                "x2": 60,
                "y2": 190,
                "color": "red",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 170,
                "text": "plane − wind = 450",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "red",
                "change": "add",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Back against the wind takes 4 hours.",
          "write": "p − w = 1800 ÷ 4 = 450"
        },
        {
          "say": "Add the equations. Two p is 1050, so p is 525.",
          "write": "p = 525 km/h"
        },
        {
          "say": "So the wind is 75 kilometres per hour.",
          "write": "w = 75 km/h"
        },
        {
          "say": "With the flow, add. Against it, subtract."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Define your pronumerals first, with units.",
          "write": "let … ="
        },
        {
          "say": "Use the same units everywhere. Don't mix cents and dollars."
        },
        {
          "say": "Reread the question. Answer what was actually asked."
        },
        {
          "say": "Minus 3 tickets, or 4.5 people? That means a mistake.",
          "write": "sense check"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Let, write, solve, answer, check.",
          "write": "let → write → solve → answer → check"
        },
        {
          "say": "Count and value. How many, and how much.",
          "write": "count + value"
        },
        {
          "say": "On a graph, the crossing point is where costs are equal.",
          "write": "cross = equal"
        },
        {
          "say": "Always check against the story.",
          "write": "check ✓"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
